Subject: [PATCH 5.10.y 0/6] can: backport of the per-device receive list lock series

This series backports the following upstream commits to 5.10.y, which
failed to apply to the 5.10-stable tree:

  962947b69589 ("can: replace ARPHRD_CAN type checks with can_get_ml_priv()")
  0f3ad9ab40e3 ("can: protect the receive lists with a per-device lock")
  43c973a0887d ("can: raw, isotp: copy socket options outside of lock_sock()")

They build on each other and have to be applied in this order. This
series answers all three FAILED mails:

  <20261109202741-failed-5.10-962947b69589@kernel.org>
  <20261109202746-failed-5.10-0f3ad9ab40e3@kernel.org>
  <20261109202744-failed-5.10-43c973a0887d@kernel.org>

Patches 1-3 are prerequisites for 5.10: commit ee8b94c8510c ("can: raw:
fix receiver memory leak") and its follow-up fixes 11c9027c983e ("can:
raw: fix lockdep issue in raw_release()") and c275a176e4b6 ("can: raw:
add missing refcount for memory leak fix") are in 5.15 and newer, but
never made it into 5.10. The per-device lock and socket option patches
rely on the ro->dev reference introduced by them. With these three
patches the raw.c changes of patches 4-6 match the 5.15 backport.

The adaptations to this tree are described in each patch. The series
applies on top of linux-5.10.y plus the already queued patches

  874f5f14cf62 ("can: isotp: check the return values of can_rx_register() in isotp_bind()")
  12297f855bbd ("can: proc: reset pkg_stats atomics individually")
  01b19ed9fa03 ("can: proc: skip stats calculation after reset in can_stat_update()")

and builds without errors or warnings after each patch.

Eric Dumazet (1):
  can: raw: fix lockdep issue in raw_release()

Oliver Hartkopp (4):
  can: raw: add missing refcount for memory leak fix
  can: replace ARPHRD_CAN type checks with can_get_ml_priv()
  can: protect the receive lists with a per-device lock
  can: raw, isotp: copy socket options outside of lock_sock()

Ziyang Xuan (1):
  can: raw: fix receiver memory leak

